    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Preterm birth may have reduced during the pandemic, especially spontaneous preterm births, but there was no difference in stillbirths. The reduction in preterm birth was only noted in single-­center studies and in unadjusted estimates, raising the possibility of referral bias. Further studies from countries with high prevalence are needed and this review will be updated periodically.",
