    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_20",
      "quote": "As the findings have changed between the review published recently and this current review, there is a need for this type of living systematic review that can be updated regularly.",
      "reason": "Explains the importance and need for conducting the review due to evolving evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": "Recently, Chmielewska 59 et al reported results from a systematic review and meta-­analyses including studies assessing population-­level impact during the pandemic period published up to January 8, 2021. They reported no difference in the PTB rate... With the availability of data from 13 more studies... the results have remarkably changed... However, this is the main reason for conducting this as a living systematic review...",
      "reason": "Identifies and cites a previous similar review and explains the need for the current update with new data."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review is not of intervention effects; it observationally compares pandemic vs. pre-pandemic periods without evaluating an intervention."
    },
    {
